Wikia has decided that new wikis will get the Monaco skin, and that eventually
MonoBook (the Wikipedia look) will not be available as a default skin on any of
their wikis.  You'll still be able to set it in your own settings, but of course
that will only work if you log in.

Wikihack is an older wiki and its MonoBook setting is grandfathered in, but the
word over there is that will go away soon.  They plan eventually to have all
wikis default to the Monaco theme.

If you are logged in, you should see at the top right of the screen, next to
your user name, a "my preferences" link.  Click on that and then choose the
"Skin" tab.  You can then see various versions of the Monaco and Quartz skins,
or you can choose MonoBook to go back to the Wikipedia look.  You can preview or
set the skin permanently.

One of the Wikia admins gave us the heads up at

http://nethack.wikia.com/wiki/Forum:Main_page_and_skin_changes

I pointed her at RGRN but I don't know if she has Usenet access.  Those with
opinions on this matter might want to let her know.



